cts and try to  remember if it's like those like  parasites that were like infected by the  t-virus but they're there they get up in  your face and they can basically plant  bugs inside your stomach and one of the  ways to stop that from happening because  that's a status condition is to eat an  herb and so yeah that's like one of the  big risks right you're in this infested  substation it was totally different it  was an interesting way to take on sort  of an event for the original and and and  expand it making it like this  interesting set piece that was spooky  and had me like really leaning on sort  of like my headphone audio to be like  are you come for the left or the right I  was behind me I don't know I think  you're in front of me I looked you're  scattering you're skittering over there  the corner if resi all three can  capitalize on that and and and kind of  feature those iconic moments while just  having all these different things in  between like man am I gonna be so  excited to just see what this is it's  it's it already seemed so promising just  based on some of the things that I've  been able to experience from it just in  the two hours that I've been playing  so resident evil 3 remake plays like  resin evil to remake right it's built on  the same engine the re engine but like  the original there's like an increase in  action right there's it's emphasized  that much more I mean cuz look you're  out on the city streets there are  zombies everywhere and so you kind of  have to literally use your ammo and your  resources a butt ton like it's just  there you are challenged to confront  enemies much more than you did in  resonable 2 we make you know we get more  ammo for example but another big  important addition this time around is  that you have a Dodge maneuver that  allows you to dodge in sort of any  direction in order to sort of jukka past  zombies this is also kind of cool  because if you time it correctly you can  do what's called a perfect dodge which  is got a little bit like the original  they had that kind of element in it but  that dodge mechanic from that game but  in this one when you do perfect dodge  zero will just like roll to the side and  then she'll like instantly like aim at a  zombie's head in slow motion it's kind  of like vanquish if you know that game  it's as you can kind of tell a lot more  action-oriented just in general across  the board that said even though there's  a emphasis on action it's still spooky  Resident Evil it's still hey we're not  gonna give you all the ammo like wasn't  evil to make you have to do a lot of  sort of risk reward management  decision-making as you're exploring this  hectic environment if anything the  action focus isn't so much that there's  just a butt ton of zombies you feel very  empowered it's that you are just  engaging with enemies more you're  engaging with having to deal with how am  I gonna get past this threat and so  that's what I mean it's elevated in that  sense it's it's less like let's go  through a hallway oh my god one zombie  how am I gonna get through this it's  more like oh my gosh I'm on the street  there are five zombies there and there's  a zombie over there and I think there's  one behind me  so I feel like this conversation  wouldn't be complete without talking  about the Nemesis which has returned  which is like ah mr. X like from resin  able to we make but more aggressive  nemesis you'll you'll come out  eventually has to be expected and he's  interesting because like mr. X he will  pursue you and try to hit you and try to  you know get in your face but the  difference is with mr. X there's evil to  remake you could mostly get past them  pretty easily right you know like oh I  see you over there  there's a desk I'm gonna run in this  direction good luck going around it I'm  gonna buy some time and get out of your  face was there a present evil 3 remake  nemesis is ridiculous and how fast he  can be he can catch up to you very  quickly in the sense of like you're just  running ahead and you think that like ah  yeah he's not gonna punch me  no he punches you  like when you see him and you choose to  run away he can instantly just like jump  right in front of you the moment you  tried to make a beeline for an exit and  it's ridiculous like he'll just knock  over zombies in front of you if they  happen to be in the path this is kind of  where the action also comes into play  right they're still managing your  resources but you're dealing with the  dude who you know to be honest you have  to you have to engage with him he is way  more aggressive he'll catch up to you  incredibly quickly and so this becomes a  part of the whole decision-making  process when you're fighting nemesis  it's a fun sort of mix a fun little sort  of iteration really on mr. X in the  sense of like you have to fight him  there are times when you know I was  confronted with this choice of like okay  I need to get to this train station  right now but he's in the way I need to  throw a grenade because like I can't  deal with this I'm running out of herbs  and first-aid sprays and ammo  so let us know in the comments below if  your is just as I am about resonable 3  remake and of course stay tuned for more  content around the game coming soon at  GameSpot once again I'm Matt thank you  for watching stars
 

